cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ContextGuard: Privacy-Preserving, Context-Aware Intrusion Reasoning for a Laptop Webcam"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ahmed
    given-names: Bakul
    email: cyberbokul@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/BakulBd/ContextGuard"
url: "https://github.com/BakulBd/ContextGuard"
abstract: >-
  ContextGuard is a CPU-only, privacy-preserving physical-security monitoring
  pipeline for a single laptop webcam. It detects and tracks people with
  YOLO26n and ByteTrack, reasons about user-defined zones and temporal
  context (dwell time, loitering, repeat visits, after-hours activity),
  scores each situation with a swappable and explainable risk engine
  (hand-tuned rules, model-derived weights, or logistic regression) compared
  against naive baselines, stores structured events in a local SQLite
  database, and generates grounded natural-language narratives validated by a
  hallucination checker. Anonymous tracking is the default; no cloud
  inference is used in the default path. Human and machine interfaces are
  provided via a Streamlit dashboard and an optional FastAPI REST service.
keywords:
  - computer vision
  - object detection
  - object tracking
  - YOLO
  - ByteTrack
  - intrusion detection
  - video surveillance
  - privacy-preserving machine learning
  - edge AI
  - CPU inference
  - anomaly detection
  - context-aware computing
  - explainable AI
  - grounded text generation
  - hallucination detection
  - natural language query
  - small language models
